  "title": "Enovate daily position report (DPR), circulated by hand for approval",
  "task_class": "pnl_reporting",
  "label_mechanical": "P&L and position reporting requests: distribute report / daily / enovate",
  "narrative": {
    "what_happens": "Someone assembles the Enovate daily position report for a given flow date and mails it out as a preliminary version \u2014 the subject line carries the date, as in \"Prelim Enovate DPR for 3-8-2001\". Recipients are asked to review and approve it; one message says plainly \"For your approval\", and two of the messages in this group are the approvals coming back. The same pattern extends to a related Enovate P&L note. Distribution is by email to a list rather than through a reporting system, and on at least one occasion the file had to be re-sent in a different form because the original was locked (\"As requested, here is an unprotected copy\"). The cycle closes when the preliminary figures are acknowledged and the report goes to the wider distribution.",
    "where_it_stalls": "No waiting, rework, deadline or manual-transfer signals were measured here, so the evidence does not show a chase or a redo loop. What it does show is a distribution problem: the report exists as an attachment that must be mailed, approved by reply, and occasionally re-issued in an unprotected copy before recipients can use it, and one instance went to a large distribution list by hand. Who owns assembly of the underlying figures is not visible in these messages.",
    "why_it_recurs": "The DPR is dated per flow day, so a new preliminary version is produced and re-circulated for approval every cycle, to a standing set of recipients.",
    "automation_opportunity": "A scheduled job that generates the dated DPR, posts it to a shared location in an unprotected readable form, and mails the standing list a link with a one-click approval, so the preliminary-then-approved cycle is recorded rather than replayed in replies.",
    "coherence": "tight"
  },
